  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, you are required to file an income tax return if you have taxable income. The deadline for filing is typically on or before April 15 of the following year.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 23 establishes the general principle of income taxation, indicating that individuals must report their income. Section 51 specifies the filing deadlines, which generally fall on April 15 for individual taxpayers. This means that if you earned income during the previous calendar year, you must file your return by this date.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor individuals earning income, it is crucial to prepare and submit your income tax return by April 15 to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. Ensure that you have all necessary documentation ready to accurately report your income and any deductions or credits you may be eligible for.",
